B.Sx=s(["Direction and distance","The colour of the flowers","Tomorrow\u2019s weather"],t.s)
B.a7q=new A.ds("What does the dance in the hive show?",B.Sx)
B.Yb=s(["A longer straight part","Louder buzzing","More dancers"],t.s)
B.a7p=new A.ds("What marks a long journey in the dance?",B.Yb)
B.ZM=s([B.a7q,B.a7p],t.rs)
B.a7Q=new A.fT("A honey bee visits several thousand flowers in a single day. Back in the hive she performs a dance that tells the others which direction the flowers lie in and how far away they are. The longer the straight part of the dance lasts, the longer the journey. For one jar of honey the bees of a colony together fly further than once around the earth.",B.ZM)
B.RE=s(["By their pattern of flashes and pauses","By the colour of the tower","By the height of the lamp"],t.s)
B.a7s=new A.ds("How do two lighthouses differ?",B.RE)
B.XV=s(["It gathers the light into one beam","It turns the light red","It measures the wind"],t.s)
B.a7n=new A.ds("What does the lens do?",B.XV)
B.Z0=s([B.a7s,B.a7n],t.rs)
B.a7P=new A.fT("A lighthouse does more than say that land is here. Every tower has its own pattern of flashes and pauses, and that pattern is printed on the sea chart. A sailor approaching a coast at night counts the seconds between two flashes and knows exactly which tower is ahead. Inside, the lens turns slowly around the lamp and gathers the light into a single beam.",B.Z0)
B.Vt=s(["A screen","A hot stone","A wooden board"],t.s)
B.a7C=new A.ds("What were the fibres dried on?",B.Vt)
B.X5=s(["Because the fibres get shorter each time","Because the colour turns grey","Because water is missing"],t.s)
B.a7y=new A.ds("Why is fresh material added?",B.X5)
B.Tb=s([B.a7C,B.a7y],t.rs)
B.a7J=new A.fT("Paper began long ago in China with plant fibres that were beaten small, stirred into water and left to dry on a screen. That is still the core of the process today; only the machines have grown. Used paper can go through the cycle several times, but the fibres get shorter with every round. That is why some fresh material is added each time.",B.Tb)
B.X3=s(["Twice","Once","Four times"],t.s)
B.a7A=new A.ds("How often a day does the sea rise and fall?",B.X3)
B.Tw=s(["About fifty minutes","About five minutes","About three hours"],t.s)
B.a7x=new A.ds("By how much does high water shift each day?",B.Tw)
B.Rf=s([B.a7A,B.a7x],t.rs)
B.a7I=new A.fT("The moon pulls at the water of the earth, and so the sea rises and falls twice a day. Because the moon reaches the same point a little later each day, high water also shifts by about fifty minutes daily. When the sun lines up with the moon, the difference is especially large. In narrow bays the water piles up higher than on an open coast.",B.Rf)
B.WN=s(["Two","One","Five"],t.s)
B.a7w=new A.ds("How many seeds does a fruit usually hold?",B.WN)
B.a_3=s(["During roasting","During picking","During drying"],t.s)
B.a7z=new A.ds("When does the taste appear?",B.a_3)
B.YC=s([B.a7w,B.a7z],t.rs)
B.a7H=new A.fT("The coffee plant carries red fruit, and each fruit usually holds two seeds. The seeds are dried and later roasted; only the roasting creates the taste we know. The darker the roast, the stronger the result and the less of the fine acidity remains. Grinding is best done shortly before brewing.",B.YC)
B.U1=s(["At the magnetic north pole","At the geographic north pole","Always east"],t.s)
B.a7m=new A.ds("Where does the needle point?",B.U1)
B.Wy=s(["Iron or strong motors nearby","Cold weather","Very bright light"],t.s)
B.a7r=new A.ds("What makes the needle useless?",B.Wy)
B.ZV=s([B.a7m,B.a7r],t.rs)
B.a7L=new A.fT("A compass needle is a small magnet that lines itself up with the magnetic field of the earth. It does not point at the geographic north pole, though, but at the magnetic one, and that one wanders from year to year. Anyone navigating precisely has to allow for the difference. Near iron or strong motors the needle becomes useless, because it follows the nearest magnet instead.",B.ZV)
